1
00:00:00,581 --> 00:00:05,137
An agent saying done is not the same as a customer accepting the work.

2
00:00:05,567 --> 00:00:12,987
Open Work Proof Settlement connects a bounded task, signed delivery evidence, and a separate decision to release

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:13,605
escrow.

4
00:00:14,035 --> 00:00:18,806
This demonstration uses Solana Devnet and DemoUSD test tokens.

5
00:00:20,804 --> 00:00:24,312
Start with a small coding task: fix an arithmetic mean.

6
00:00:24,742 --> 00:00:30,615
The work order freezes the source revision, permitted file, tests, parties, and budget.

7
00:00:31,059 --> 00:00:35,293
The customer funds one DemoUSD before execution.

8
00:00:37,266 --> 00:00:41,083
In the first recorded case, DeepSeek proposed the fix.

9
00:00:41,527 --> 00:00:49,148
Open Work Proof protected the read and patch operations, and Docker verification checked the immutable tests.

10
00:00:49,605 --> 00:00:56,500
The customer can inspect the actual change and signed evidence, instead of relying on a chat message saying

11
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,642
the job is finished.

12
00:00:59,636 --> 00:01:02,162
Passing tests does not move the tokens.

13
00:01:02,619 --> 00:01:06,558
The customer reviews the delivery and signs an acceptance message.

14
00:01:07,001 --> 00:01:11,074
That signature records a decision; it is not a payment transaction.

15
00:01:13,037 --> 00:01:17,889
Release is a second wallet approval, co-signed by the designated attester.

16
00:01:18,346 --> 00:01:25,725
The finalized transaction transferred exactly one DemoUSD to the provider and left the vault empty.

17
00:01:26,155 --> 00:01:28,709
Only then did the application show settled.

18
00:01:30,812 --> 00:01:36,497
Now look at a separate order, using a clearly labelled reference patch, not another model call.

19
00:01:36,941 --> 00:01:40,691
Verification passed, but the customer rejected the delivery.

20
00:01:41,107 --> 00:01:43,889
A separate transaction recorded the dispute.

21
00:01:44,320 --> 00:01:47,532
Release was blocked, and the token stayed in escrow.

22
00:01:47,962 --> 00:01:50,879
Rejection alone did not automatically refund it.

23
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:58,861
The demo provider then consented to cancellation, and the customer co-signed the refund.

24
00:01:59,318 --> 00:02:05,500
The finalized transaction returned exactly one DemoUSD to the original customer.

25
00:02:05,944 --> 00:02:10,420
The vault became empty, and the provider's balance did not increase.

26
00:02:10,850 --> 00:02:15,138
Terminal guards also refused another refund or release.

27
00:02:17,145 --> 00:02:18,193
The boundaries matter.

28
00:02:18,623 --> 00:02:25,545
The chain enforces permissions and transfers; a trusted application attester checks the evidence.

29
00:02:25,976 --> 00:02:33,220
Noncustomer roles are app-owned, the program is upgradeable, and there is no automatic arbitration or real-money

30
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:33,610
claim.

31
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:40,559
Open Work Proof Core predates this competition; this entry adds the settlement integration.

32
00:02:41,002 --> 00:02:46,540
Verification, acceptance, and settlement remain three distinct events.
